# Lexus LS400 four-door saloon, 1990-1994.
#
# The car that launched Lexus: 5,000 mm long, 1,830 mm wide, 1,410 mm high,
# 2,850 mm wheelbase; 4.0 V8, rear-wheel drive, air suspension optional. Built to
# undercut the S-Class and 7-series and a small but significant British import.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lexus_LS
#
# Colours: Black, Silver, Blue and Grey are documented Lexus colours of the period.
#
# Weight: 20 in total (black 7, silver 6, blue 4, grey 3).
#
# Speed 250 km/h; comfort 145/395 (line). Class 4.
# Dates: 1990-1994 with a road tail to about 2006.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/lexus-ls400.blend. References:
# citycars/references/lexus-ls400/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.
#
# Gate C, 2026-11-16: accepted as built. Known deviation: angular low-poly body and
# simple rectangular lamp units, as with the other order-23 cars; silhouette, glass
# band (26-27% of height) and proportions match. No correction round.

obj=citycar
